  "summary": "Screened all 52 clients across updates, local performance, drift, feature summaries and subgroup outcomes (Sex, AgeGroup, Income), then confirmed with narrower queries. The budget is fully spent (20.0 used).\n\nFindings:\n- WI, HI and SC show the clearest fault: consistently anomalous uploads (update norms about 3.2\u20133.5x the median, strongly negative cosine to the median update, z of about -15 to -17) while local AUC and calibration look normal. This fits poisoning (scaled, sign-flipped updates). Onset is taken as round 1, but per-round onset was not verified.\n- GU is a moderate-confidence prevalence_shift lead: observed prevalence is well above predicted from round 1, with normal AUC. It is a small client and the evidence is weaker.\n\nDismissed leads: NC (GenHlth tail), ND (HighChol spread) and DC (BMI mean, Smoker) looked anomalous in the broad feature screen, but the narrower round-20 query showed normal values, so they were treated as screening noise. Several subgroup O/E outliers (MO, WV Income group 6; WI AgeGroup 1; DC AgeGroup 3) and some drift onset flags were not confirmed and were not reported; their deviations are at or below about z_noise 5 and the budget did not allow follow-up."
